  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of Alaska Medicaid Prolia and Xgeva (denosumab), a RANKL inhibitor, in a single Prolia pack. Version 1; Original: 12/16/21; Approval: 1/21/22; Effective: 3/1/22.",
    "Closed indications imply product and attest to the listed diagnosis. Approval criteria and shared denial exclusions are encoded; denial criterion 1 is covered by approval clauses. Prolia risk documentation is a single-choice attestation of any qualifying branch; overlapping qualifying findings need only one selection.",
    "Source ambiguity: Xgeva approval #2 reads a OR; b AND; c. Encoded as SRE OR (HCM AND bisphosphonate step), so #2c applies only to HCM. GCT is a separate age \u226512 path. SRE has no additional bisphosphonate requirement.",
    "Initial approval up to 6 months; reauthorization up to 12 months if bone improvement and/or stabilization (notes only).",
    "Quantity limits (notes only): Prolia 60 mg/1 mL, 1 syringe every 6 months; Xgeva 120 mg/1.7 mL, load 4 vials per 28 days \u00d71 dose then maintenance 1 vial monthly. HCPCS J0897.",
    "Cautions: see package inserts https://www.pi.amgen.com/~/media/amgen/repositorysites/pi-amgen-com/prolia/prolia_pi.pdf and https://www.pi.amgen.com/~/media/amgen/repositorysites/pi-amgen-com/xgeva/xgeva_pi.pdf.",
    "PDL status unknown: source is silent. Skeletal maturity accepts yes or its UI-normalized boolean true.",
    "Remaining gaps: documentation verification, authorization duration, reauthorization response, dosing, quantity enforcement and package-insert cautions require manual review."
  ],
